+# Capacity: what this service costs, and what it stops doing first
+
+The page a person reads before they raise a limit, add a subscriber or promise a customer a
+throughput number. Everything in it comes from a load run that can be repeated: the generator, the
+percentiles and the curve are `relay/2.20-load-testing`, and the run is one command.
+
+This is the skeleton: the sections are the ones a capacity question needs, and every link is a
+placeholder until the step's last task is done — `kiln check relay/2.20-load-testing` runs the
+`links` gate over this file, and it fails while the targets are `TODO`.
+
+## Method
+
+How the numbers below were produced: [which command](TODO), on [what machine](TODO), with
+[which settings](TODO). A number without its method is a rumour.
+
+## Measurements
+
+| concurrency | p99 | backlog | growth over the level below |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| [from the run](TODO) | | | |
+
+## The slope
+
+What the growth column means, and where the curve stops being a curve: [what the queue does
+first](TODO).
+
+## Workers and throughput
+
+What adding a worker buys, and what it costs: [measured here](TODO).
+
+## What this is not
+
+[what the run does not measure](TODO) — and the one level below it that would.
